**Answer: G) ≈ 120.28 (heat‑units / hr · ft), ≈ 499.9 °F at the pipe‑insulation interface**

**Explanation**

1. **Geometry (per foot of pipe)**  

| Quantity | Value (ft) |
|----------|------------|
| Inner radius of steel pipe \(r_i\) | \( \frac{6}{2}\text{ in}=3\text{ in}=0.25\) |
| Outer radius of steel pipe \(r_o\) | \( \frac{6.5}{2}\text{ in}=3.25\text{ in}=0.270833\) |
| Inner radius of insulation \(r_{i,ins}=r_o\) | 0.270833 |
| Outer radius of insulation \(r_{o,ins}\) | \(3.25\text{ in}+3.5\text{ in}=6.75\text{ in}=0.5625\) |

2. **Thermal resistances (cylindrical conduction, length = 1 ft)**  

\[
R_{\text{steel}}=\frac{\ln\!\left(\dfrac{r_o}{r_i}\right)}{2\pi k_{\text{steel}}}
               =\frac{\ln(1.08333)}{2\pi(26)}
               =\frac{0.08004}{163.363}=4.9\times10^{-4}\;\text{(hr·ft·°F)/heat‑unit}
\]

\[
R_{\text{ins}}=\frac{\ln\!\left(\dfrac{r_{o,ins}}{r_{i,ins}}\right)}{2\pi k_{\text{ins}}}
              =\frac{\ln(2.0775)}{2\pi(0.04)}
              =\frac{0.7309}{0.25133}=2.907\;\text{(hr·ft·°F)/heat‑unit}
\]

\[
R_{\text{total}} = R_{\text{steel}}+R_{\text{ins}}
                 \approx 2.9075\;\text{(hr·ft·°F)/heat‑unit}
\]

3. **Heat‑loss rate**  

\[
\dot Q = \frac{T_{\text{inner}}-T_{\text{outer}}}{R_{\text{total}}}
       = \frac{500^\circ\!F-150^\circ\!F}{2.9075}
       \approx 1.20\times10^{2}
\]

\[
\boxed{\dot Q\;\approx\;1.20\times10^{2}\ \text{heat‑units per hour per foot}}
\]

(rounded to 120.28 in the answer list).

4. **Temperature at the pipe‑insulation interface**  

The temperature drop across the steel wall is  

\[
\Delta T_{\text{steel}} = \dot Q\,R_{\text{steel}}
                        \approx 120.28 \times 4.9\times10^{-4}
                        \approx 0.059^\circ\!F
\]

Hence  

\[
T_{\text{interface}} = T_{\text{inner}}-\Delta T_{\text{steel}}
                     \approx 500^\circ\!F - 0.059^\circ\!F
                     \approx 499.94^\circ\!F
\]

Rounded to the values given in the options, this is 499.88 °F.

Therefore the combination that matches both the heat‑loss rate and the interface temperature is **option G**.

